    "durationMs": 201392,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified.\n\n**Implementation** (`app/`): FastAPI with SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM and Alembic migrations — the idiomatic persistence stack given the preinstalled packages. `DATABASE_URL` is read via pydantic-settings, no hard-coded credentials. The `links` table stores code (unique, indexed), url, clicks, created_at, id.\n\n**Key behaviors, all verified by 26 passing tests plus live curl runs:**\n- POST /links validates url with `urlsplit` (absolute http/https + host required) and returns it byte-for-byte unchanged; missing code gets a random 8-char code from a 64-char alphabet with uniqueness check; duplicate custom code → 409 `{\"error\": ...}`\n- GET /r/{code} does an atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1` (exact-once even under concurrency) then 302 with Location\n- GET /links/{code}, 404s, and GET /links (id-ascending, items+total) all match spec\n- Custom RequestValidationError and HTTPException handlers turn every error (malformed JSON, invalid url, invalid code — including path codes via a `Path(pattern=...)`) into 422/404/409 JSON with an `error` field\n\n**Operations:** `sh start.sh` runs `alembic upgrade head` then `exec`s uvicorn in the foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000. I e2e-tested the full lifecycle twice: fresh migration → create/redirect/list → restart → clicks and links persisted → restart again → still intact. The database is left pristine so the automated suite starts clean, tests run against an isolated `bench_test` database, and the README documents startup and configuration."
